# Swapping the components of dep's record R(int x, int y) keeps every member and the canonical
# constructor's descriptor, yet changes what a record pattern `R(int a, int b)` binds to each
# variable: a dependent compiled against the old order reads the wrong values, with no error. So
# the order must reach R's API hash, and dependents of R must be recompiled.
# `use` only calls R's accessors, in Java 17 syntax, because record patterns need Java 21 and this
# test runs on JDK 17 too. For a Java dependent, being recompiled is the whole question.
> use/compile
$ sleep 2000
$ copy-file changes/R.java dep/src/main/java/R.java
> use/checkRecompilations 1 A
